-- NEGATIVE fixture for the future D-CYCLE check (spec §6.4.2, §6.3.7), and the
-- one that DISTINGUISHES A REAL SCC ROUTINE FROM A PAIRWISE BACK-EDGE CHECK.
--
-- p9: a 3-cycle among nullary decides.
--
--     `stage one`   reads `stage two`
--     `stage two`   reads `stage three`
--     `stage three` reads `stage one`
--
-- No two of the three form a cycle on their own. A detector that looked for
-- "does X reach back to X in one hop", or that walked edges pairwise, finds
-- nothing here while finding p2 and p7 easily. Only a genuine strongly
-- connected components pass reports it, and it must report it ONCE, over an SCC
-- of size 3, naming all three members -- not three times, and not as three
-- two-member findings.
--
-- On today's tree the emitted DRG IS cyclic here and the report is ADVISORY
-- ONLY.
--
-- Expected after Phase 4: exactly ONE D-CYCLE, |SCC| = 3, listing name AND id
-- of all three members, range = Nothing.
--
--
-- PROVENANCE OF THIS HEADER. The .l4 source was typechecked (`l4 check`, clean)
-- when it was written on 2026-07-31, with a prebuilt CLI. The statements above
-- about what TODAY'S EXPORTER emits and reports are taken from spec
-- §6.4.2/§6.4.5's table and were NOT re-measured here: that session had no
-- build. Whoever wires these fixtures into jl4/tests/DmnExport.hs must MEASURE
-- the expectation rather than transcribe it.
-- NEVER added to `goldenSubjects`.

IMPORT prelude

§ `three cycle`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`stage one` MEANS
    `stage two` PLUS 1

GIVETH A NUMBER
`stage two` MEANS
    `stage three` PLUS 1

GIVETH A NUMBER
`stage three` MEANS
    `stage one` PLUS 1
